## Third-party components and references

OpenMesh is an independent implementation. It contains no code from the projects below; they
were studied as prior art and for hardware pin-map facts, and are credited here.

- Reticulum / LXMF / LXST — Mark Qvist (https://reticulum.network/). LXST and its Rust port
  rsLXST are under a restrictive licence and are NOT used.
- Ratspeak and rsReticulum/rsLXMF — https://ratspeak.org/ (Reticulum Licence). Their Rust
  architecture informed OpenMesh's client/daemon split.
- Meshtastic firmware (GPL-3.0) — board pin maps and variant files were consulted to cross-check
  hardware wiring for the reference boards; OpenMesh board headers are written independently and
  cite the vendor documentation.
  The PlatformIO board definitions in `firmware/boards/pio/*.json` and the nRF52 Arduino board
  variants in `firmware/variants/*/` are derived from meshtastic/firmware (GPL-3.0). They are
  included here under GPL-3.0 terms, which AGPL-3.0 permits (GPLv3 §13 / AGPLv3 §13); they are
  configuration files only and contain no Meshtastic application logic. If this distinction
  matters to you, the files are isolated under those two directories.
- MeshCore (https://meshcore.io/) — protocol design inspiration (repeater/room-server roles).
- Semtech AN1200.13/AN1200.22 — LoRa airtime formulas.

Rust crates are licensed under their respective terms (Apache-2.0/MIT/BSD), listed in each
crate's Cargo metadata. Firmware libraries (RadioLib, Adafruit nRF52 core, arduino-esp32) are
licensed by their authors; see `firmware/THIRD_PARTY.md` when added.
